      "value": "Another way I thought about accomplishing this is for groups to be able to promote other groups' instances. It would list them just the same as other instances in that group (maybe unless you're in the promoted group), but identifying what group the instance is actually for.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-02-10T04:23:45.216Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This is mainly for creators: DJs, singers, musicians and other performers or entertainers. Artists can use their Groups to send notifications when they're performing, but often the performance itself happens on another group's instance As such, they're still compelled to accept friend requests from people who want to attend their events, making their Friend Lists a bit of a nightmare, while also cutting people who're too shy to send friend invites off (yes there's some of those).\n\nFollowing someone instead of adding them as a friend would help keep Friend Lists manageable while still allowing fans and supporters to join their favorite performers. A follower would have to be allowed to join only if the followed user is on Blue, or a special, new status. That'd also allow performers to avoid having to be on Orange if they want their actual friends to join them.\n\nObviously, it should be an opt-in feature.\n\nThe idea was given to me by MissStabby.\n\nA post was submitted in 2019 for something that may look similar, but is actually about receiving updates on new Worlds uploaded by a creator, which is different, and can be achieved to some extend with Groups. There's that post: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/follow-creators",
